# C8 anion addition: BINDING ENERGY of HOO- in the cavity (within-model).
#
# Goal: is the HOO- bound in the catalyst cavity relative to HOO- free in water?
# The DIRECT subtraction complex - free_cat - free_HOO failed badly (+/-hundreds
# of kJ/mol) because the complex's HOO- is embedded in the 116 MM host and no
# free 3-atom reference reproduces that embedding; changing the free reference
# from CPCM to ddCOSMO alone moved it by 343 kJ/mol.
#
# So take the difference WITHIN the same 133-atom QM/MM model: hold C128...O130
# at increasing separation and relax; the host, its point charges and the
# solvation model are identical at every point, so they cancel and the plateau
# energy IS the separated reference.
#
#   dE_bind = E(rs_anion, C...O 2.93 A) - E(plateau, C...O ~8-10 A)
#
# Seed = rs_anion with the HOO- rigidly pulled to C128...O130 = 4.0 A, so step 1
# is close to the seed. Scan 4 -> 10 A in 1 A steps; steps past ~8 A should
# plateau (HOO- out of contact) -- that plateau is the reference.
#
# NOTE dE_bind is electronic + host relaxation ONLY. The free anion's
# translational entropy is not in the model (the HOO- is boxed in both states),
# so a standard-state term (~+20-30 kJ/mol) is added on top for a solution
# binding free energy.
#
# NO Calc_Hess (scan Hessian bug). Charge convention: QM region charge on the
# *xyzfile line; Charge_total = whole system. QM -1, host 0, total -1.
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) Opt TightOpt TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{55 58 61 64 120 121 122 123 124 125 126 127 128 129 130 131 132}
END
Charge_total -1
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
  Scan
    B 128 130 = 4.0, 10.0, 6
  end
  MaxIter 500
end

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile -1 1 job.xyz
